# Cart and Checkout Rules

- Cart display prices are hints; Checkout recalculates authoritative totals server-side.
- Checkout submission requires `Idempotency-Key`; retries must not create duplicate orders or reservations.
- Pipeline order: validate cart -> validate offers -> price/tax/shipping/promotions -> reserve inventory -> create order(s) -> create payment intent(s).
- Multi-vendor carts may produce multiple orders; never merge vendor financial state in one aggregate mutation.
- Failed checkout must release inventory reservations per compensating policy.
- Never trust browser-calculated discounts, tax, shipping, or grand totals.
- Checkout orchestrates Order and Payment through application ports only.
- Persist immutable snapshots on orders at creation time.
- Guest cart → authenticated cart **merge must run server-side** (concurrency-safe). Never merge only in browser state or localStorage.
